<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n6971" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνα-μάσσω</span></b> , 
			Att.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνά-ττω</span></b> , fut.
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ξω</span> (v. infr.): (v. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μάσσω</span>):—<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>rub</i> or <i>wipe off,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔργον, ὃ σῇ κεφαλῇ
			ἀναμάξεις</span> a deed (as if a stain), which thou <i>wilt
				wipe off</i> with or on thine own head (since it was believed
			that the pollution of murder was avoided by wiping the weapon on the
			victim's head), <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				19.92
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ μὲν ἐμῇ κεφαλῇ ἀναμάξας φέρω</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					1.155
				</span></i>
			:—
				Med.
			, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀσέβειαν δημοσία -ξασθαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Paus.
					10.33.2
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀναματτομένη τῷ προσώπῳ τοῦ
				αἵματος</span>
			<i>having</i> [some of] the blood <i>wiped on her</i> face,
				<i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Ant.</u>
				77
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ ἑτέρου κακόν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ph.
					2.379
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ψυχὴ ἀ. πάθος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					J.
					<u>AJ</u>
					16.8.5
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοσαύτας ἀναμεμαγμένος κηλῖδας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Porph.
					<u>Chr.</u>
					88
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			
				Med.
			, <i>knead one's bread,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Nu.</u>
				676
			</span></i> codd., cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>AB</u>
				391
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>receive an impression,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Ti.Locr.
				94a
			</span></i>; of the eyes, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. τοὺς τύπους τῶν ὁρωμένων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arr.
					<u>Epict.</u>
					2.23.3
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ ψυχὴ ἀναμάττεσθαι δύναται τοὺς τῶν
					αἰσθητῶν τύπους</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plot.
					4.3.26
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. τὸ εἶδος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Alex.Aphr.
					<u>de An.</u>
					137.1
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<i>obtain an impression of,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὴν ψυχήν τινος διὰ τῶν λόγων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Eun.
					<u>Hist.</u>
					p.266D.
				</span></i>
			
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>4.</b>
			<i>refurbish,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὴν μνήμην</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Max.Tyr.
					8.2
				</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
